{
  "id": "COMPOUND:20368 - PROTEIN:6138",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 5,11-Dihydroxy-3,3-dimethylpyrano[3,2-a]xanthen-12-one may interact with the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This compound is implicated in targeting Caspase-5, which is a key enzyme in the apoptotic pathway. Caspase-5 is further targeted by WS-5995 B and 5-Oxobrucine, both of which are linked to the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Caspase-5 and ultimately on the proteasome subunit indicates a possible role for this compound in modulating proteasome activity, potentially through the inhibition of Caspase-5 or its downstream signaling. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between the compound and the proteasome subunit, though the exact mode of interaction remains to be elucidated. The observed scores suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of the compound in proteasome regulation.",
